1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,856
My skin was pure white until the day I lied about my mother's cooking, and it turned gray.

2
00:00:06,156 --> 00:00:12,708
At first, I thought it was a rash. Then I lied to my boss about traffic, and my entire neck darkened.

3
00:00:13,008 --> 00:00:22,032
Every small untruth added another layer of charcoal to my body. Society quickly invented a cruel name for us.

4
00:00:22,332 --> 00:00:30,852
The Stainers. We were the walking archives of deceit. We couldn't hide behind smiles anymore because our faces betrayed us.

5
00:00:31,152 --> 00:00:38,520
I swore I would never speak another falsehood. I became obsessively honest, keeping my chest pale and clear.

6
00:00:38,820 --> 00:00:45,564
Until tonight. My sister stood in my kitchen, begging to know if her runaway husband was safe.

7
00:00:45,864 --> 00:00:52,416
I knew he was dead. I had found his car in a ravine three days ago. But I looked into her eyes.

8
00:00:52,716 --> 00:00:59,196
And I smiled. I lied, telling her he called me from another state, just to spare her breaking heart.

9
00:00:59,496 --> 00:01:06,936
The moment the lie left my lips, a sharp burning spread across my chest. I rushed to the bathroom.

10
00:01:07,236 --> 00:01:14,388
My entire body turned pitch black. The biggest lie of my life wasn't a sin; it was pure love.
